WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.145
Step 1. Open the specimen definitions list.

1.2
00:00:03.145 --> 00:00:07.858
A specimen definition records what staff collect, how they collect it,

1.3
00:00:07.858 --> 00:00:10.685
and how the laboratory keeps the specimen.

1.4
00:00:10.685 --> 00:00:15.023
In Settings, under Clinical, select Specimen Definitions.

2.1
00:00:15.023 --> 00:00:19.354
Step 2. Start a new definition. Select Add Definition.

2.2
00:00:19.354 --> 00:00:23.406
Care opens the Create Specimen Definition form.

3.1
00:00:23.406 --> 00:00:28.568
Step 3. Fill in the basic information. Enter the Title and the Description.

3.2
00:00:28.568 --> 00:00:36.526
Care fills in the Slug from the title and selects Active as the status.

4.1
00:00:36.526 --> 00:00:41.176
Step 4. Add the specimen details. Type Collected is required.

4.2
00:00:41.176 --> 00:01:02.940
Care uses these details when staff collect a specimen for a service request.

5.1
00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:05.930
Step 5. Add the type tested information.

5.2
00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:09.492
Care fills in Is Derived, Single Use and Preference,

5.3
00:01:09.492 --> 00:01:18.111
and the other fields are optional. You can also describe the container.

6.1
00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:21.300
Step 6. Save the definition. Select Save.

6.2
00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:25.459
Care shows Specimen definition created and opens the list.

6.3
00:01:25.459 --> 00:01:31.192
If another definition uses the same slug, change the slug and save again.
